## Preserved exact verifier findings

- `PTM-F001` exact verifier reason: “The migration uses literal backslash-escaped quotes inside a C# raw string and lacks visible MigrationAttribute/model snapshot; no live PostgreSQL execution was available.” Acceptance was executable PostgreSQL SQL, EF discovery from the configured migrations assembly, production `MigrateAsync()` only, and provider-independent registration tests. It was completed in `b20efa6 fix(timeline): register executable PostgreSQL migration`.
- `PTM-F002` exact verifier reason: “Hosted admin/participant buttons are alerts, artifact input has no upload handler, and timeline UI only adds entries.” Acceptance was authorized admin user CRUD/deactivation with optional password reset, participant list/add/update/remove, timeline and entry load/create/update, artifact upload/list/download, and profile/recovery workflows. It was completed in `92bc8c0 fix(timeline): complete hosted workflow operations`.
- `PTM-G001` exact verifier finding: “`/api/auth/recovery` remains only an acknowledgement endpoint: it ignores the request and returns a generic message, with no expiring one-time recovery token/state, secure token persistence, configurable local outbox delivery, reset endpoint, or hosted request/reset journey.” It was completed by `8a42376 fix(timeline): complete recovery and administrator access`.
- `PTM-G002` exact verifier finding: “Administrators can list all projects, but descendant checks (`CanReadProject`, `CanWriteProject`, `CanManageProject`) do not special-case the Administrator role, so an administrator who neither owns nor participates in a project is denied access to participants, timelines, entries, and artifacts.” It was completed by the same commit.

